        "rationale": "`requirements.layout.project.workspace` has two observable obligations. The workspace must have exactly two first-party packages, `habeas` and `trust-but-verify`. Those packages must sit at the repository root and in `crates/trust-but-verify/`. The test `tests/repository.rs#fn[workspace_contains_frontend_and_sdk_but_not_the_vendor_fork]` is marked `{test}` for the subject, and it covers both obligations.\n\n- **Exact set of members:** The test runs `cargo metadata --no-deps --locked --offline`. It filters the packages to `workspace_members`, sorts their names, and asserts equality with `[\"habeas\", \"trust-but-verify\"]`. A third member, a missing member, or a vendor fork that is a member would fail this assertion.\n- **Location of `trust-but-verify`:** The test asserts that `crates/trust-but-verify/src/lib.rs` exists. It also asserts that the root `Cargo.toml` depends on `trust-but-verify` with `path = \"crates/trust-but-verify\"`. Cargo treats a path dependency inside the workspace root as a member. A `trust-but-verify` package placed elsewhere would therefore either break this path or add a third member, and either case fails the test.\n- **Location of `habeas`:** The test reads a root `Cargo.toml` that has `[dependencies]`, so the root is itself a package. The root depends on `trust-but-verify`, so it cannot be that package. With exactly two members, the root package must be `habeas`.\n\nThe test never compares each member's manifest path directly. I did not count this as a gap, because the checks above rule out the plausible violations."
